  "description": "Typewriter Grunge is a bold vintage display font inspired by classic typewriters, aged ink prints, and worn paper textures. Designed with authentic distressed details, this font perfectly recreates the nostalgic look of old typewritten documents while adding a rugged handcrafted feel that makes every design stand out.\nIts rough texture and bold slab serif style make it ideal for projects that require a rustic, retro, industrial, or vintage aesthetic. Whether you’re designing posters, book covers, branding, logos, apparel, labels, packaging, café menus, whiskey labels, newspaper headlines, social media graphics, or printable crafts, Typewriter Grunge delivers a timeless character full of personality.\nThe authentic weathered effect gives each letter the appearance of naturally worn ink, making it perfect for western themes, historical projects, detective stories, old manuscripts, rustic branding, vintage advertisements, and creative editorial layouts. Despite its distressed appearance, the font remains highly legible, making it suitable for both large headlines and eye-catching display text.",
  "fullDescription": "<p>Typewriter Grunge is a bold vintage display font inspired by classic typewriters, aged ink prints, and worn paper textures. Designed with authentic distressed details, this font perfectly recreates the nostalgic look of old typewritten documents while adding a rugged handcrafted feel that makes every design stand out.</p>\n<p>Its rough texture and bold slab serif style make it ideal for projects that require a rustic, retro, industrial, or vintage aesthetic. Whether you’re designing posters, book covers, branding, logos, apparel, labels, packaging, café menus, whiskey labels, newspaper headlines, social media graphics, or printable crafts, Typewriter Grunge delivers a timeless character full of personality.</p>\n<p>The authentic weathered effect gives each letter the appearance of naturally worn ink, making it perfect for western themes, historical projects, detective stories, old manuscripts, rustic branding, vintage advertisements, and creative editorial layouts. Despite its distressed appearance, the font remains highly legible, making it suitable for both large headlines and eye-catching display text.</p>",
